Problem: Minimum Common Value (LC 2540)

Pattern: Two Pointers

Approach:

1. Initialize two pointers, i and j, at the beginning of the two sorted arrays.
2. Compare the elements at both pointers.
3. If both elements are equal, return that element because it is the smallest common value.
4. If the element in the first array is smaller, move pointer i forward.
5. If the element in the second array is smaller, move pointer j forward.
6. Repeat until a common value is found or either pointer reaches the end of its array.
7. If no common value is found, return -1.

Time Complexity: O(n + m)

Space Complexity: O(1)